+    /// so preflight/disable and shutdown all succeed -- but for every `GetTemperatures` request
+    /// pushes an unsolicited `TemperatureUpdate` alternating the left reading between two values
+    /// far enough apart to individually pass [`is_valid_baseline_reading`] (both are well inside
+    /// `MIN_WATER_CENTIDEG..=MAX_WATER_CENTIDEG`) but whose spread exceeds
+    /// `BASELINE_MAX_SPREAD_CENTIDEG` -- so baseline collection reaches `BASELINE_MIN_SAMPLES`
+    /// quickly, but `validate_baseline`'s stability check genuinely fails. Proves item 6 end to
+    /// end: rejected for real instability, not for a missing/unsupported reading.
